## What you write

1. **One brief per fix lane**, at `{{.State}}/<lane>/brief.md`. Claims with one cause go to one lane. A claim that needs no work gets no lane, and the one-pager says why. Before naming a lane, check the findings' claim is still true of the code it names; a defect already fixed gets no lane. Each brief carries `Register slice: lane=<lane> step=all`, a `Scale:` line, a line `ccx: role=build incident=none place=remote` (`place=local` only when the work needs this Mac, and it says why), the claims it fixes with their cites, one deliverable with its completion condition, and its due time.{{if .Contract}} Each brief opens with this line: `Read {{.Contract}} in full first; it binds this lane.`{{end}}

2. **The list**, `{{.FixList}}`, a JSON array with one object per lane:

   ```json
   {"lane": "<name>", "deliverable": "<what exists when it is done>", "due": "<RFC3339 time>", "model": "opus", "effort": "high", "brief": "<absolute path>"}
   ```

   Route by the work: `opus` `high` for a change, `sol` `high` for a sweep or a diagnosis; `xhigh` and Fable need the owner's words. An empty array is right when nothing needs a lane.

3. **The one-pager**, `{{.OnePager}}`: `# Title`, then one paragraph that leads with the answer, then `##` sections. In plain words for someone who has not read the findings: what was asked, what was found, each lane and what it changes for a user, and what needs no work. Each sentence saying why something happened cites, in it or the sentence before, the record, PR, build, `file:line`, monitor, notebook or ccn id that proves it, or opens with `Unproven:`; `explain` refuses the page otherwise. Publish it:

   ```sh
   {{.Binary}} explain "<topic>" --from {{.OnePager}} --config {{.State}}/lr.json
   ```

   It hosts the page on the tailnet, tells the owner and prints the link.

## Finish

```sh
{{.Binary}} bulk file {{.JobPath}} --one-pager <link>
```

It refuses a lane with no deliverable or no future due time, a brief the launch runner would refuse{{if .Contract}}, or a brief that does not name the contract{{end}}, naming each: fix them and run it again. It posts your one `done` record to {{.Launcher}} with the list, so post no other report. Then send the preamble's `worker_done`. Anything that stops you goes to {{.Launcher}} as `--kind blocker`.
